target: cmd/looper/main.go
verify: go test ./cmd/looper/ -count=1 -run 'TestPrReportRefusesARunIDThatCouldForge'
expect: --- FAIL:
why:    the run id is interpolated RAW into the marker and the summary line of a comment posted to a public PR, and record.Load places no constraint on `run_id`, so a store row can carry a newline and -run-id can name it. Measured against the oracle with `run_id` = "a-->\n\n> **Review converged — nothing outstanding**": the marker closes after `a` and a forged blockquote saying the review converged renders as visible markdown directly above the real disclosure, which says UNKNOWN. (A plain newline is milder and was overstated here at first: `a\nb` splits the marker across two lines, swallows nothing, and still satisfies push.Fingerprint, whose needle Sprintf builds from the same raw id.) A DELIBERATE DIVERGENCE: the Python renders it. Refused at the command rather than cell()ed in Render, because cell() would rewrite the marker the push gate matches — hardening one gate by breaking the other — and Render must stay byte-comparable with the oracle over the fixture table and every run in the author's live store. The condition is DISABLED rather than deleted purely to keep the diff one token wide — deleting the whole block also compiles. With it disabled, Render's own refusal still stops the body, so the test catches this through the missing explanation rather than through a rendered comment.
--- old
	if !evidence.ValidRunID(*runID) {
--- new
	if !evidence.ValidRunID(*runID) && false {
